  <data name="TestData_Examples_Button" xml:space="preserve"><value>Examples</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Test data examples</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_GeneralTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Basic rules</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_GeneralDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each [group name] starts one test case. Names such as [1], [01], and [3-b3-01] are all valid; case numbers follow text order only. Ordinary text after the group header is passed to the program unchanged, while ordinary # comments are ignored. Select Save after editing to update the cache.</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_3B3Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Example 1: standard input</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_3B3ExampleNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>(using 3-b3 as an example)</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_3B3Description" xml:space="preserve"><value>The program reads one floating-point number per run, so place one input value on the line below each group header. The next group header ends the previous case and starts another.</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_3B3Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Blank lines are preserved as input. Add one only when the program really needs a blank line to simulate Enter, not merely for visual spacing.</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_TcTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Example 2: command-line arguments</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_TcDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>When txt_compare needs no standard input, put its full command line in # @args: after the group header. Paths containing spaces must be quoted; the directive itself is not passed to stdin.</value></data>
  <data name="TestData_Examples_TcNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>The two cases above use normal and detailed display modes. Replace the sample paths with real files; Demo and student programs always receive the same arguments.</value></data>
